    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d182">

                <pb facs="0300" n="230" sameAs="frus:frus1862/pg230"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr. Adams.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 387.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1862-11-04"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >November</hi> 4, 1862.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Your despatches by the Arabia are received,
                    but there is not time for special notice of them before the closing of the
                    mail.</p>
                <pb facs="0301" n="231" xml:id="pg231"/>
                <p>All our land and naval operations are going on with vigor. Those who in Europe
                    have supposed that this government is either idle or ineffective will be
                    undeceived in time, I trust, to abate their desires for measures which would
                    bring the two continents into collision upon a question which belongs chiefly to
                    America, but on which both continents ought to be agreed.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Francis Adams,</hi> Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
